          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20916 dkms: detect --enable-gss as last configure option",
        "message": "LU-20916 dkms: detect --enable-gss as last configure option\n\nThe DKMS configuration checks for \"--enable-gss\" in the configure\noptions using the regex '--enable-gss[^-]'. This requires a character\nafter \"gss\", so it fails to match when \"--enable-gss\" is the last\nargument in the options string. As a result, ptlrpc_gss is silently\nomitted from the DKMS module list, and loading it later fails with:\n\n  modprobe: FATAL: Module ptlrpc_gss not found in directory\n  /lib/modules/<kernel-version>\n\nChange the regex to '--enable-gss($|[^-])' so that it also matches at\nthe end of the string, while still excluding longer options such as\n\"--enable-gss-keyring\".\n\nApply the fix to both debian/dkms.conf.in and\nlustre/scripts/dkms.mkconf.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manhong Dai <manhong.dai@netapp.com>\nChange-Id: I7799480b6463022ac9ca20e8c55794ccf6bee58f\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
